<description>
Expand a diagonal-index color table by cycling its non-black header sequence.

Input structure
- The input is a nonempty square grid.
- The top row and left column are the same header sequence.
- Every cell is the header color at index max(row, column); black header cells
  appear only as a trailing blank suffix.

Rule
- Drop the trailing black blanks from the header.
- Repeat the remaining header colors until it is twice as long as the input side.
- Fill the doubled square so each cell again takes the repeated header color
  at index max(row, column).

Key insight
- The visible pattern is not a 2D tile; it is a one-dimensional header sequence
  projected through the max(row, column) diagonal-index rule.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "top row/left column header sequence of the diagonal-index table, ignoring trailing black blanks",
  "transform": "cycle the active header to twice the input side length and fill each output cell with header[max(row, column)]",
  "grid_shape": "square with input side length multiplied by 2"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, side N = 4-7 [observed N=5]
  header:
    definition: top row and left column are identical sequences of length N
    active_prefix: first K non-black colors, K = N-1 to N (trailing blacks = 0-1)
    colors: all non-black, 2-5 distinct colors, may repeat consecutively
  fill_rule: cell (r,c) = header[max(r,c)]
  output:
    size: 2N x 2N
    extended_header: active prefix cycled to length 2N
    fill_rule: same max(r,c) indexing with extended header

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (no inversion needed; input is fully determined by header)
  steps:
    1. pick grid side N in 4-7
    2. pick trailing_blacks in {0, 1}; active_length K = N - trailing_blacks (require K >= 2)
    3. build active header of length K from non-black colors; allow consecutive repeats but ensure >=2 distinct colors
    4. append trailing_blacks zeros to get full header of length N
    5. fill NxN grid via cell(r,c) = header[max(r,c)]
    6. output is not generated (solver produces it)
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

